 "_role_nouns": "v79.12.1 (E2): the capitalised words that are never a party's surname when printed alone right before the saving clause «, a prescindere dalla titolarità» -- a party's or an office's role, an act, a body, a region. rulings.name_spans redacts such a lone word (rule «saving») unless it is here, in «words» or among the «openers»; a wrong redaction (logged with its rule) is fixed by adding its word here. v79.12.3 (item 7): also the words never read as a surname alone right after an article or an articled preposition written out (rule «article»: «il Rossi», «del Bianchi», «dal Verdi», «la Russo» are redacted; «il Ricorrente», «il Notaio», «il Giudice», «l'Imputato», «il Teste», «la Sentenza» stay) -- the parties' and offices' roles, the acts, a few countries, titles and institutional adjectives; the gazetteer («words»: «il Tribunale», «la Corte», «il Pubblico Ministero», «la Cassazione», «il Codice», «la Legge») and the openers stay too. Each such redaction is logged with rule «article» and its word: a wrong one is fixed by adding the word here. v79.12.5 (review of item 7): the roles, acts and bodies the rule «article» was found to redact on synthetic probes (Responsabile, Condannato, Contribuente, Segretario, Revisore, Conducente, Lodo, Dispositivo, Svolgimento, Visto …), the words of the acts' and offices' names that follow an articled preposition (Consumo, Strada, Navigazione, Privacy, Concorrenza, Mercato, Crisi, Imposte, Redditi, Ministri), the months, the weekdays and the feasts, the unions' acronyms.",
